-- 1. First Light — Dawn. The yard switches on; nobody is in a hurry.
-- Eval 00-setup.tidal first.
-- ~40 cycles (~100 s at 96 BPM).
-- The first switch, a boot on concrete, a low G add9, then the work song on the
-- piano. Sparse by design: let the room and the objects arrive one at a time.

glideBpm 96 16
-- clear anything left from the previous piece
fadeSilence 8 [1,2,3,7,8,9]

-- the first switches
d3 switchOn
-- a boot on concrete
d1 bootDawn
-- the bass finds the floor
d6 bassLight

-- the work song, first time: piano high, unaccompanied
d5 $ motifPiano # amp 0.2

-- low G add9, still dark
d4 $ slow 2 $ pianoPedal (slow 4 hLight) # amp 0.3

-- a brush, half-awake
xfadeIn 1 24 $ stack [bootDawn, brushSoft]
-- the yard breathes
xfadeIn 10 32 $ stack [air, windBed]
xfadeIn 9 32 $ degradeBy 0.6 gravel
